Fixed. All tests pass.

**Cause:** In `discover/runner.go`, `filterIntegratedGPUs` drops integrated GPUs unless explicitly enabled via `OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE`, with `integratedGPUAllowedByDefault` as the allowlist — which only permitted `CUDA` devices. The Radeon 8060S (ROCm, `gfx1151`) was therefore filtered out by default.

**Fix** (`discover/runner.go:412`): extended the allowlist to also admit ROCm integrated GPUs with the `gfx1151` compute target:

```go
func integratedGPUAllowedByDefault(device ml.DeviceInfo) bool {
	if device.Library == "CUDA" {
		return true
	}
	// Allowlist AMD integrated GPUs with a supported compute target (e.g. Radeon 8060S).
	return device.Library == "ROCm" && device.GFXTarget == "gfx1151"
}
```

This matches the test expectations: `gfx1151` (8060S) admitted, `gfx1103` (780M) still dropped in auto mode, and explicit `OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE` true/false overrides unchanged.

`go test ./discover/...` → `ok`
